-- חוזר הממונה על השכר 2023-1-12 (20.3.2023) — תשלום מקדמה לעובדים במגזר
-- הציבורי בשל ההבנות על הסכם המסגרת
-- An advance on the one-time grant the coming framework agreement is to
-- pay: who is an "employee" for it, the amount M = A × B × C, its
-- clarifications (unpaid leave, the coronavirus exception, hourly and daily
-- pay), its gross treatment, its deduction, the employee on leave when it
-- is paid, the approvals for other public bodies, and the annex of
-- qualifying grades.

IMPORT prelude
IMPORT daydate
IMPORT common

§ `תשלום מקדמה לעובדים במגזר הציבורי בשל ההבנות על הסכם המסגרת`

-- akn:hc_1/p1 akn:hc_1/p2 akn:hc_1/p3 akn:hc_1/p4 The date (20.3.2023), the circular's number, the addressee (the Deputy Accountant-General) and the subject line; no rule.

-- akn:hc_1/p5 The recital: on 27.2.2023 the State and the Histadrut reached understandings on the principles of a framework collective agreement to be signed with the State and other public employers; no rule of its own.

-- akn:hc_1/p6 The recital: the coming agreement is expected to pay a one-time grant, and since it is not yet signed, the circular gives instructions for an advance on the rules understood for that grant; the advance's rules follow in sections 1-6.

DECLARE `advance party` IS ONE OF
    `the State as employer`
    `a public-sector body`
    `the Wage Controller`

DECLARE `advance action` IS ONE OF
    `pay the advance` HAS `advance amount paid` IS A NUMBER
    `make provident-fund contributions on the advance`
    `deduct the advance from the salary`
    `notify the Wage Controller in writing of the payment`

-- Time in the regulative rules below is counted in months from 1.3.2023:
-- the March 2023 salary is paid in April (month 1), the June 2023 salary in
-- July (month 4).
`the month the March 2023 salary is paid` MEANS 1
`the month the June 2023 salary is paid`  MEANS 4

§§ `1(א) "עובד"`

@desc A State employee, as far as the advance asks about them.
DECLARE `advance employee` HAS
    `employed in the State service on 1.3.2023`                IS A BOOLEAN
    `paid under the agreements of a qualifying grade`          IS A BOOLEAN @desc salary computed under the collective agreements of a grade the Histadrut represents and annex A lists (the "qualifying grades")
    `employed in the State service on 1.6.2022`                IS A BOOLEAN
    `left the service between 1.6.2022 and 28.2.2023`          IS A BOOLEAN @desc employment ended at any point of the qualifying period
    `in qualifying grades throughout 1.6.2022 to 28.2.2023`    IS A BOOLEAN @desc graded in one or more qualifying grades for the whole qualifying period
    `on unpaid leave in the qualifying period`                 IS A BOOLEAN @desc spent part of 1.6.2022-28.2.2023 on unpaid leave, or leave treated as unpaid leave, for any reason
    `the grade sent employees on unpaid leave for the coronavirus` IS A BOOLEAN @desc the employee's grade is one whose employees were sent on unpaid leave because of the coronavirus (section 1(ב)(2))
    `months of the calculation period`                         IS A LIST OF `calculation month`

-- §1(א)(1): employed on 1.3.2023, paid under a qualifying grade's agreements.
@ref akn:hc_1__para_1__subpara_a akn:hc_1__para_1__subpara_a__cls_1
GIVEN e IS AN `advance employee`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `meets §1(א)(1)` e IF
        e's `employed in the State service on 1.3.2023`
    AND e's `paid under the agreements of a qualifying grade`

-- §1(א)(2) with its continuity rules. (ב): reserve duty, birth and
-- parenthood under the Women's Employment Law, and sick leave under
-- takshir 33.210 (full, half or no pay) count towards continuity; ¶2: an
-- absence approved by the employer and paid (rest leave, paid study) does
-- not break it. These are employment, so only leaving the service, a
-- non-qualifying grade, or (on one reading) unpaid leave can break it.
-- (א): unpaid leave periods "are not taken into account" in computing the
-- continuity. F-2023-03-20_sachar_2023-1-12_mikdama-misgeret-c: that reads
-- two ways — the period is skipped and the continuity runs across it, or
-- it is not employment and so breaks the continuity.
@ref akn:hc_1__para_1__subpara_a__cls_2 akn:hc_1__para_1__subpara_a__cls_2/p2 akn:hc_1__para_1__subpara_a__cls_2__pnt_b akn:hc_1__para_1__subpara_a__cls_2__pnt_b/p2
GIVEN e IS AN `advance employee`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `employed continuously, unpaid leave skipped` e IF
        e's `employed in the State service on 1.6.2022`
    AND NOT e's `left the service between 1.6.2022 and 28.2.2023`
    AND e's `in qualifying grades throughout 1.6.2022 to 28.2.2023`

@ref akn:hc_1__para_1__subpara_a__cls_2__pnt_a
GIVEN e IS AN `advance employee`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `employed continuously, unpaid leave breaking it` e IF
        `employed continuously, unpaid leave skipped` e
    AND NOT e's `on unpaid leave in the qualifying period`

-- The reading adopted (F-2023-03-20_sachar_2023-1-12_mikdama-misgeret-c): unpaid leave breaks the continuity. It is
-- the literal one: (א) and (ב) are a pair, and what (ב) "takes into
-- account" — periods counted as employment — (א) does not; ¶2 says that a
-- PAID absence does not break the continuity, which says something only if
-- an unpaid one does.
@export The test of section 1(א) of Wage Controller circular 2023-1-12: is a State employee an "employee" entitled to the March 2023 advance on the framework agreement's one-time grant
GIVEN e IS AN `advance employee` @desc the State employee
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `an employee for the advance` e IF
        `meets §1(א)(1)` e
    AND `employed continuously, unpaid leave breaking it` e

§§ `1(ב) The amount: M = A × B × C`

@ref akn:hc_1__para_1__subpara_b/p4
`A` MEANS 6000

-- B: the months employed in the calculation period, 1.10.2020-31.3.2023,
-- divided by 30.
@ref akn:hc_1__para_1__subpara_b/p5
`the calculation period begins` MEANS Date 1 10 2020

@ref akn:hc_1__para_1__subpara_b/p5
`the calculation period ends` MEANS Date 31 3 2023

@ref akn:hc_1__para_1__subpara_b/p5
`the months of the calculation period` MEANS 30

DECLARE `kind of month` IS ONE OF
    `month worked`
    `month of paid absence`                                    @desc an absence approved by the employer and paid, such as rest leave or paid study
    `month of reserve duty, birth and parenthood or sick leave` @desc reserve duty; birth and parenthood under the Women's Employment Law 1954; sick leave under takshir 33.210, with full, half or no pay
    `month as an employee in arrangement`                      @desc defined as "עובד בהסדר" under the collective agreement of 16.9.2020
    `month of unpaid leave`                                    @desc unpaid leave, or leave treated as unpaid leave, for any reason

@desc One calendar month of the calculation period in which the employee was employed or on leave.
DECLARE `calculation month` HAS
    `month begins`                IS A DATE
    `share of the month`          IS A NUMBER @desc 1 for a whole month; for part of a month, the days employed divided by the work days of that month (section 1(ב), the paragraph after B)
    `month kind`                  IS A `kind of month`
    `position fraction that month` IS A NUMBER @desc the share of a full position held that month; for an employee in arrangement, as the agreement of 16.9.2020 computes it for its special payment; for hourly or daily pay, the auxiliary fraction of section 1(ב)(3)

-- ¶6 of 1(ב): a month employed in part counts as the days employed divided
-- by the work days of that month.
@ref akn:hc_1__para_1__subpara_b/p6
GIVEN `days employed` IS A NUMBER, `work days of the month` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A NUMBER
DECIDE `the share of a partly employed month` `days employed` `work days of the month` IS
    `days employed` DIVIDED BY `work days of the month`

-- The work days in a stretch of days, for a workplace whose week ends on a
-- given weekday (Sunday = 0): Thursday (4) for five days a week, Friday (5)
-- for six. The circular names no holidays; none falls in the month used below.
GIVEN d IS A NUMBER, `last day` IS A NUMBER, `last weekday` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A NUMBER
DECIDE `work days from` d `last day` `last weekday` IS
    IF d GREATER THAN `last day`
    THEN 0
    ELSE (IF `Weekday of` d AT MOST `last weekday` THEN 1 ELSE 0)
         PLUS `work days from` (d PLUS 1) `last day` `last weekday`

-- §1(ב)(1)(א)-(ב) and its ¶¶2-3: for B and C unpaid leave is left out;
-- reserve duty, birth and parenthood, sick leave, a period as an employee in
-- arrangement, and a paid approved absence are counted. (¶3 says the paid
-- absence is counted "in the qualifying period"; outside it, it is still a
-- month in which the employee was employed in the State service, which is
-- what B and C count.)
@ref akn:hc_1__para_1__subpara_b/p14 akn:hc_1__para_1__subpara_b__cls_1 akn:hc_1__para_1__subpara_b__cls_1__pnt_a akn:hc_1__para_1__subpara_b__cls_1__pnt_b akn:hc_1__para_1__subpara_b__cls_1__pnt_b/p3
GIVEN m IS A `calculation month`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `counted for B and C` m IF
    CONSIDER m's `month kind`
    WHEN `month of unpaid leave` THEN FALSE
    OTHERWISE TRUE

-- §1(ב)(2): for the number of months in B, and for that only, unpaid leave
-- from 1.10.2020 to 30.6.2021 is counted too — only for a grade whose
-- employees were sent on unpaid leave for the coronavirus; agreed with the
-- Histadrut as an exception that sets no precedent.
@ref akn:hc_1__para_1__subpara_b__cls_2
`the coronavirus window ends` MEANS Date 30 6 2021

@ref akn:hc_1__para_1__subpara_b__cls_2
GIVEN e IS AN `advance employee`, m IS A `calculation month`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `counted for B` e m IF
        `counted for B and C` m
    OR  (    e's `the grade sent employees on unpaid leave for the coronavirus`
         AND m's `month begins` AT LEAST `the calculation period begins`
         AND m's `month begins` AT MOST `the coronavirus window ends`)

@ref akn:hc_1__para_1__subpara_b/p5
GIVEN e IS AN `advance employee`
GIVETH A NUMBER
DECIDE `B` e IS
    sum (map (GIVEN m YIELD m's `share of the month`)
             (filter (GIVEN m YIELD `counted for B` e m) (e's `months of the calculation period`)))
    DIVIDED BY `the months of the calculation period`

-- C: the average position fraction over the months counted for it, each
-- month weighted by the share of it employed (a whole month weighs 1).
@ref akn:hc_1__para_1__subpara_b/p7 akn:hc_1__para_1__subpara_b__cls_1__pnt_b/p2
GIVEN e IS AN `advance employee`
GIVETH A NUMBER
DECIDE `C` e IS
    IF `months weighed` EQUALS 0
    THEN 0
    ELSE sum (map (GIVEN m YIELD m's `share of the month` TIMES m's `position fraction that month`) `the months for C`)
         DIVIDED BY `months weighed`
    WHERE
        `the months for C` MEANS filter (GIVEN m YIELD `counted for B and C` m) (e's `months of the calculation period`)
        `months weighed`   MEANS sum (map (GIVEN m YIELD m's `share of the month`) `the months for C`)

-- §1(ב)(3)(א): an hourly-paid employee (students, for instance): the
-- average monthly hours in the months counted for C, divided by 182.
@ref akn:hc_1__para_1__subpara_b__cls_3 akn:hc_1__para_1__subpara_b__cls_3__pnt_a
GIVEN `average hours a month` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A NUMBER
DECIDE `the auxiliary position fraction for hourly pay` `average hours a month` IS
    `average hours a month` DIVIDED BY 182

-- §1(ב)(3)(ב): a daily-paid employee: the average monthly days worked,
-- divided by 20.83 in a five-day workplace or by 25 in a six-day one.
@ref akn:hc_1__para_1__subpara_b__cls_3__pnt_b
GIVEN `average days a month` IS A NUMBER, `days in the working week` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A NUMBER
DECIDE `the auxiliary position fraction for daily pay` `average days a month` `days in the working week` IS
    IF `days in the working week` EQUALS 6
    THEN `average days a month` DIVIDED BY 25
    ELSE `average days a month` DIVIDED BY 20.83

-- "סכום M יעוגל לשקל החדש השלם הקרוב": to the nearest whole shekel. The
-- circular names no rule for an exact half; it is rounded up here.
@ref akn:hc_1__para_1__subpara_b/p13
GIVEN x IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A NUMBER
DECIDE `to the nearest shekel` x IS
    FLOOR (x PLUS 0.5)

@ref akn:hc_1__para_1__subpara_b akn:hc_1__para_1__subpara_b/p2 akn:hc_1__para_1__subpara_b/p3
GIVEN b IS A NUMBER, c IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A NUMBER
DECIDE `M for` b c IS
    `to the nearest shekel` (`A` TIMES b TIMES c)

@export default The advance (in shekels, gross) a State employee is paid with the March 2023 salary under Wage Controller circular 2023-1-12, on the framework agreement's coming one-time grant; 0 if not an "employee" under its section 1(א)
GIVEN e IS AN `advance employee` @desc the State employee, with every month of 1.10.2020-31.3.2023 in which they were employed or on leave
GIVETH A NUMBER
DECIDE `the advance` e IS
    IF `an employee for the advance` e
    THEN `M for` (`B` e) (`C` e)
    ELSE 0

§§ `1 Payment, 2 gross, 3 deduction, 4 leave at payment`

-- §1: paid with the March 2023 salary, which is paid in April 2023.
@ref akn:hc_1__para_1
GIVEN e IS AN `advance employee`
GIVETH A DEONTIC `advance party` `advance action`
DECIDE `paying the advance` e IS
    IF `an employee for the advance` e
    THEN PARTY `the State as employer`
         MUST  `pay the advance` paid
               PROVIDED paid AT LEAST `the advance` e
         WITHIN `the month the March 2023 salary is paid`
         LEST  BREACH BY `the State as employer` BECAUSE "§1: the advance is paid with the March 2023 salary"
    ELSE FULFILLED

-- §2: the advance is paid gross, and no provident-fund contributions
-- (training fund, pension fund, managers' insurance) are made on it.
@ref akn:hc_1__para_2
GIVETH A DEONTIC `advance party` `advance action`
DECIDE `no contributions on the advance` IS
    PARTY `the State as employer`
    SHANT `make provident-fund contributions on the advance`
    WITHIN `the month the June 2023 salary is paid`
    LEST  BREACH BY `the State as employer` BECAUSE "§2: no provident-fund contributions are made on the advance"

-- §3: deducted when the June 2023 salary is paid or when the one-time grant
-- of the coming agreement is paid, whichever is earlier, subject to the
-- Wage Protection Law 1958.
@ref akn:hc_1__para_3
GIVEN `the month the grant is paid` IS A NUMBER @desc months from 1.3.2023 to the payment of the one-time grant; not known when the circular was written
GIVETH A NUMBER
DECIDE `the deduction month` `the month the grant is paid` IS
    min `the month the June 2023 salary is paid` `the month the grant is paid`

@ref akn:hc_1__para_3
GIVEN `the month the grant is paid` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A DEONTIC `advance party` `advance action`
DECIDE `deducting the advance` `the month the grant is paid` IS
    PARTY `the State as employer`
    MUST  `deduct the advance from the salary`
    WITHIN `the deduction month` `the month the grant is paid`

-- §4: an employee on birth and parenthood, or on sick leave without pay,
-- when the advance is paid, is paid it with the first salary after
-- returning to work, and no later than the next one — provided that date
-- comes before the deduction of §3.
@ref akn:hc_1__para_4
GIVEN e IS AN `advance employee`, `the first salary after return` IS A NUMBER, `the month the grant is paid` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A DEONTIC `advance party` `advance action`
DECIDE `paying the advance after leave` e `the first salary after return` `the month the grant is paid` IS
    IF      `an employee for the advance` e
        AND `the first salary after return` LESS THAN `the deduction month` `the month the grant is paid`
    THEN PARTY `the State as employer`
         MUST  `pay the advance` paid
               PROVIDED paid AT LEAST `the advance` e
         WITHIN `the first salary after return` PLUS 1
         LEST  BREACH BY `the State as employer` BECAUSE "§4: the advance is paid with the first salary after the return, or the next one at the latest"
    ELSE FULFILLED

-- akn:hc_1__para_5 The circular was coordinated with the Histadrut, which accepts it; a statement of agreement, no rule.

§§ `6 Other public-sector bodies`

DECLARE `other agreement` IS ONE OF
    `no other agreement settling pay rises for 2020-2027`
    `another agreement for part of 1.1.2020-31.12.2027`
    `another agreement for the whole of 1.1.2020-31.12.2027`

@desc A public-sector body other than the State, as far as section 6 asks about it.
DECLARE `public body` HAS
    `will sign or join the framework agreement`  IS A BOOLEAN
    `pays grades the Histadrut represents that are not qualifying` IS A BOOLEAN @desc wants to pay the advance to employees paid under Histadrut-represented grades not listed in annex A
    `its other agreement`                        IS AN `other agreement` @desc another collective agreement settling pay rises or financial benefits for 1.1.2020-31.12.2027

DECLARE `approval for a body` IS ONE OF
    `the general approval, with written notice on payment`
    `a specific approval in advance and in writing`
    `no approval under this circular`

-- §6(א): a body that is to sign the framework agreement or will join it,
-- and wants to pay its qualifying-grade employees an advance, has the Wage
-- Controller's approval to pay it under this circular. §6(ב) ¶2: to pay it
-- to non-qualifying Histadrut grades needs a specific approval in advance
-- and in writing. §6(ג): the general approval is for a body with no other
-- agreement settling pay for 1.1.2020-31.12.2027; one with another
-- agreement for part of that period needs a specific approval in advance.
-- A body with another agreement for the WHOLE period has neither route
-- (the general approval is for bodies with no such agreement, and §6(ג) ¶2
-- opens the specific route only for part of the period), so it has no
-- approval under this circular.
@ref akn:hc_1__para_6__subpara_a akn:hc_1__para_6__subpara_b/p2 akn:hc_1__para_6__subpara_c akn:hc_1__para_6__subpara_c/p2
GIVEN p IS A `public body`
GIVETH AN `approval for a body`
DECIDE `the approval a body has` p IS
    BRANCH IF (NOT p's `will sign or join the framework agreement`) THEN `no approval under this circular`
           IF p's `its other agreement` EQUALS `another agreement for the whole of 1.1.2020-31.12.2027` THEN `no approval under this circular`
           IF p's `pays grades the Histadrut represents that are not qualifying` THEN `a specific approval in advance and in writing`
           IF p's `its other agreement` EQUALS `another agreement for part of 1.1.2020-31.12.2027` THEN `a specific approval in advance and in writing`
           OTHERWISE `the general approval, with written notice on payment`

-- §6(ב): a body paying under the general approval notifies the Wage
-- Controller in writing when it makes the payment (time in months from the
-- payment).
@ref akn:hc_1__para_6__subpara_b
GIVEN p IS A `public body`
GIVETH A DEONTIC `advance party` `advance action`
DECIDE `notifying the Wage Controller` p IS
    IF `the approval a body has` p EQUALS `the general approval, with written notice on payment`
    THEN PARTY `a public-sector body`
         MUST  `notify the Wage Controller in writing of the payment`
         WITHIN 1
         LEST  BREACH BY `a public-sector body` BECAUSE "§6(ב): a body paying the advance under the general approval notifies the Wage Controller in writing with the payment"
    ELSE FULFILLED

-- akn:conclusions The sign-off (Efi Malkin, acting Wage Controller) and the copies (the Civil Service Commissioner, the chairman of the Histadrut, the public-sector employers); no rule.

§§ `נספח א' — the qualifying grades`

-- Annex A as printed: the grade and its State-service code, in the printed
-- order. The printed table has a serial-number column that the corpus
-- publishes empty (the source numbers it automatically), and its header is
-- repeated at each page break; neither carries a rule. For the jurists,
-- public defenders and state attorneys the annex excludes anyone whose
-- salary is linked to a judicial office-holder's.
@ref akn:att_1__hc_1/p1 akn:att_1__hc_1/t1
DECLARE `qualifying grade` HAS
    `grade name`  IS A STRING
    `grade codes` IS A STRING @desc the State-service code(s), "--" where the annex prints none

`the qualifying grades` MEANS
    LIST `qualifying grade` "מינהלי" "1",
         `qualifying grade` "אחיד" "2",
         `qualifying grade` "טכנאי רנטגן" "8",
         `qualifying grade` "מח\"ר, לרבות פסיכולוגים" "11, 16",
         `qualifying grade` "מהנדסים" "12",
         `qualifying grade` "טכנאים והנדסאים" "13",
         `qualifying grade` "פיזיוטרפיסטים" "20",
         `qualifying grade` "משפטנים (מובהר כי האמור לא יחול לגבי מי ששכרו צמוד לשכר נושא משרה שיפוטית)" "21",
         `qualifying grade` "סנגורים ציבוריים (מובהר כי האמור לא יחול לגבי מי ששכרו צמוד לשכר נושא משרה שיפוטית)" "25",
         `qualifying grade` "פרקליטים (מובהר כי האמור לא יחול לגבי מי ששכרו צמוד לשכר נושא משרה שיפוטית)" "22",
         `qualifying grade` "עיתונאים" "27",
         `qualifying grade` "עובדי מעבדה, ביוכימאים ומיקרוביולוגים" "33",
         `qualifying grade` "רוקחים" "34",
         `qualifying grade` "סטודנטים לרפואה ולסיעוד" "36",
         `qualifying grade` "אחים ואחיות (לרבות אחים ואחיות בריאות הציבור)" "38, 39",
         `qualifying grade` "פארה רפואיים (לרבות קלינאי תקשורת וטכנולוגים רפואיים)" "47",
         `qualifying grade` "מרפאים בעיסוק" "49",
         `qualifying grade` "מפקחים ימיים" "61",
         `qualifying grade` "מקצ\"ט" "62",
         `qualifying grade` "סטודנטים" "71",
         `qualifying grade` "מתמחים במשפטים" "81",
         `qualifying grade` "נערים עובדים וחניכים" "--",
         `qualifying grade` "קלדניות שופטים" "526",
         `qualifying grade` "מעברי הגבול" "519",
         `qualifying grade` "רשות מקרקעי ישראל" "565",
         `qualifying grade` "כבאים" "202",
         `qualifying grade` "עובדים סוציאליים" "24, 124",
         `qualifying grade` "שירות החוץ" "9",
         `qualifying grade` "יהלום" "547",
         `qualifying grade` "עוזרים משפטיים" "562",
         `qualifying grade` "יחידת הפיצו\"ח (ויחידת הפיצו\"ח 90)" "567"

GIVEN `name` IS A STRING
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `a qualifying grade by name` `name` IF
    any (GIVEN g YIELD g's `grade name` EQUALS `name`) `the qualifying grades`

-- The annex's closing note: the veterinarians' and the civil-research
-- grades are still under discussion with the Histadrut, are not listed, and
-- are paid no advance under this circular.
@ref akn:att_1__hc_1/p2
`grades excluded pending talks` MEANS LIST "הוטרינרים", "מחקר אזרחי"

#ASSERT count `the qualifying grades` EQUALS 31
#ASSERT `a qualifying grade by name` "מהנדסים"
#ASSERT all (GIVEN n YIELD NOT `a qualifying grade by name` n) `grades excluded pending talks`

§§ `Findings`

-- F-2023-03-20_sachar_2023-1-12_mikdama-misgeret-a: §1(ב)(2)'s illustration
-- prints B = 21.5/30 = 0.716, which is 21.5/30 cut at three decimals
-- (0.71666…). With B as printed, M is 4,296; with B exact, 4,300.
@ref akn:hc_1__para_1__subpara_b__cls_2__pnt_4/p5
`B as the illustration prints it` MEANS 0.716

`B as printed and B exact give different advances` MEANS
        `B as the illustration prints it` EQUALS TRUNC (21.5 DIVIDED BY 30) 3
    AND `M for` `B as the illustration prints it` 1 EQUALS 4296
    AND `M for` (21.5 DIVIDED BY 30) 1 EQUALS 4300
#ASSERT `B as printed and B exact give different advances`

-- F-2023-03-20_sachar_2023-1-12_mikdama-misgeret-b: the illustration counts
-- 15.1.2021-31.1.2021 as half a month; ¶6's rule (days employed over the
-- month's work days) gives 11/21 in a five-day workplace and 14/26 in a
-- six-day one — neither a half.
@ref akn:hc_1__para_1__subpara_b__cls_2/p2 akn:hc_1__para_1__subpara_b__cls_2/p3 akn:hc_1__para_1__subpara_b__cls_2__pnt_1 akn:hc_1__para_1__subpara_b__cls_2__pnt_2 akn:hc_1__para_1__subpara_b__cls_2__pnt_3 akn:hc_1__para_1__subpara_b__cls_2__pnt_4
`the share of January 2021 as the illustration counts it` MEANS 0.5

`January 2021 under ¶6, five days a week` MEANS
    `the share of a partly employed month`
        (`work days from` (Day (Date 15 1 2021)) (Day (Date 31 1 2021)) Thursday)
        (`work days from` (Day (Date 1 1 2021)) (Day (Date 31 1 2021)) Thursday)

`January 2021 under ¶6, six days a week` MEANS
    `the share of a partly employed month`
        (`work days from` (Day (Date 15 1 2021)) (Day (Date 31 1 2021)) Friday)
        (`work days from` (Day (Date 1 1 2021)) (Day (Date 31 1 2021)) Friday)

-- The illustration's employee, January's share given: started 15.1.2021,
-- in a grade sent on coronavirus unpaid leave, on unpaid leave in March and
-- April 2021 and from August to December 2021, otherwise at 100%.
GIVEN `January's share` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH AN `advance employee`
DECIDE `the illustrated employee` `January's share` IS
    `advance employee` WITH
        `employed in the State service on 1.3.2023`                IS TRUE
        `paid under the agreements of a qualifying grade`          IS TRUE
        `employed in the State service on 1.6.2022`                IS TRUE
        `left the service between 1.6.2022 and 28.2.2023`          IS FALSE
        `in qualifying grades throughout 1.6.2022 to 28.2.2023`    IS TRUE
        `on unpaid leave in the qualifying period`                 IS FALSE
        `the grade sent employees on unpaid leave for the coronavirus` IS TRUE
        `months of the calculation period`                         IS `the illustrated months` `January's share`

GIVEN `January's share` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A LIST OF `calculation month`
DECIDE `the illustrated months` `January's share` IS
    LIST `calculation month` (Date 1 1 2021) `January's share` `month worked` 1,
         `calculation month` (Date 1 2 2021) 1 `month worked` 1,
         `calculation month` (Date 1 3 2021) 1 `month of unpaid leave` 1,
         `calculation month` (Date 1 4 2021) 1 `month of unpaid leave` 1,
         `calculation month` (Date 1 5 2021) 1 `month worked` 1,
         `calculation month` (Date 1 6 2021) 1 `month worked` 1,
         `calculation month` (Date 1 7 2021) 1 `month worked` 1,
         `calculation month` (Date 1 8 2021) 1 `month of unpaid leave` 1,
         `calculation month` (Date 1 9 2021) 1 `month of unpaid leave` 1,
         `calculation month` (Date 1 10 2021) 1 `month of unpaid leave` 1,
         `calculation month` (Date 1 11 2021) 1 `month of unpaid leave` 1,
         `calculation month` (Date 1 12 2021) 1 `month of unpaid leave` 1,
         `calculation month` (Date 1 1 2022) 1 `month worked` 1,
         `calculation month` (Date 1 2 2022) 1 `month worked` 1,
         `calculation month` (Date 1 3 2022) 1 `month worked` 1,
         `calculation month` (Date 1 4 2022) 1 `month worked` 1,
         `calculation month` (Date 1 5 2022) 1 `month worked` 1,
         `calculation month` (Date 1 6 2022) 1 `month worked` 1,
         `calculation month` (Date 1 7 2022) 1 `month worked` 1,
         `calculation month` (Date 1 8 2022) 1 `month worked` 1,
         `calculation month` (Date 1 9 2022) 1 `month worked` 1,
         `calculation month` (Date 1 10 2022) 1 `month worked` 1,
         `calculation month` (Date 1 11 2022) 1 `month worked` 1,
         `calculation month` (Date 1 12 2022) 1 `month worked` 1,
         `calculation month` (Date 1 1 2023) 1 `month worked` 1,
         `calculation month` (Date 1 2 2023) 1 `month worked` 1,
         `calculation month` (Date 1 3 2023) 1 `month worked` 1

`the illustration's half month is not ¶6's share` MEANS
        `January 2021 under ¶6, five days a week` EQUALS 11 DIVIDED BY 21
    AND `January 2021 under ¶6, six days a week` EQUALS 14 DIVIDED BY 26
    AND NOT (`January 2021 under ¶6, five days a week` EQUALS `the share of January 2021 as the illustration counts it`)
    AND NOT (`January 2021 under ¶6, six days a week` EQUALS `the share of January 2021 as the illustration counts it`)
    AND NOT (`the advance` (`the illustrated employee` `January 2021 under ¶6, five days a week`)
             EQUALS `the advance` (`the illustrated employee` `the share of January 2021 as the illustration counts it`))
#ASSERT `the illustration's half month is not ¶6's share`

-- The encoding reproduces the illustration's own figures with its half
-- month: 21.5 months counted for B, so B = 21.5/30, and C = 1.
@ref akn:hc_1__para_1__subpara_b__cls_2__pnt_4/p2 akn:hc_1__para_1__subpara_b__cls_2__pnt_4/p3 akn:hc_1__para_1__subpara_b__cls_2__pnt_4/p4 akn:hc_1__para_1__subpara_b__cls_2__pnt_4/p6 akn:hc_1__para_1__subpara_b__cls_2__pnt_4/p7
`the illustration's B and C` MEANS
        `B` (`the illustrated employee` `the share of January 2021 as the illustration counts it`) EQUALS 21.5 DIVIDED BY 30
    AND `C` (`the illustrated employee` `the share of January 2021 as the illustration counts it`) EQUALS 1
#ASSERT `the illustration's B and C`

-- The reading adopted for F-2023-03-20_sachar_2023-1-12_mikdama-misgeret-a and F-2023-03-20_sachar_2023-1-12_mikdama-misgeret-b: B is used exact, not cut, and a
-- part month is ¶6's share; the illustration's figures are approximations.
#ASSERT `the advance` (`the illustrated employee` `the share of January 2021 as the illustration counts it`) EQUALS 4300
#ASSERT `the advance` (`the illustrated employee` `January 2021 under ¶6, five days a week`) EQUALS 4305
#ASSERT `the advance` (`the illustrated employee` `January 2021 under ¶6, six days a week`) EQUALS 4308

-- F-2023-03-20_sachar_2023-1-12_mikdama-misgeret-c: a month of unpaid leave
-- in the qualifying period decides the whole advance, one way or the other.
`an employee with a month of unpaid leave in December 2022` MEANS
    `advance employee` WITH
        `employed in the State service on 1.3.2023`                IS TRUE
        `paid under the agreements of a qualifying grade`          IS TRUE
        `employed in the State service on 1.6.2022`                IS TRUE
        `left the service between 1.6.2022 and 28.2.2023`          IS FALSE
        `in qualifying grades throughout 1.6.2022 to 28.2.2023`    IS TRUE
        `on unpaid leave in the qualifying period`                 IS TRUE
        `the grade sent employees on unpaid leave for the coronavirus` IS FALSE
        `months of the calculation period`                         IS `the illustrated months` 1

`unpaid leave in the qualifying period reads two ways` MEANS
        `employed continuously, unpaid leave skipped` `an employee with a month of unpaid leave in December 2022`
    AND NOT `employed continuously, unpaid leave breaking it` `an employee with a month of unpaid leave in December 2022`
#ASSERT `unpaid leave in the qualifying period reads two ways`

§§ `Examples`

-- §1(ב)'s own example: 24 of the 30 months at 75%: 6,000 × 24/30 × 3/4 = 3,600.
@ref akn:hc_1__para_1__subpara_b/p8 akn:hc_1__para_1__subpara_b/p9 akn:hc_1__para_1__subpara_b/p10 akn:hc_1__para_1__subpara_b/p11 akn:hc_1__para_1__subpara_b/p12
`the example's advance` MEANS `M for` (24 DIVIDED BY 30) (3 DIVIDED BY 4)
#ASSERT `the example's advance` EQUALS 3600

#ASSERT `an employee for the advance` (`the illustrated employee` 0.5)
#ASSERT NOT `an employee for the advance` `an employee with a month of unpaid leave in December 2022`
#ASSERT `the advance` `an employee with a month of unpaid leave in December 2022` EQUALS 0

-- §1(ב)(3): 91 hours a month on average is half a position; 15 days a
-- month in a six-day workplace is 0.6.
#ASSERT `the auxiliary position fraction for hourly pay` 91 EQUALS 0.5
#ASSERT `the auxiliary position fraction for daily pay` 15 6 EQUALS 0.6

#ASSERT `the deduction month` 3 EQUALS 3
#ASSERT `the deduction month` 6 EQUALS 4

`a local authority signing the agreement` MEANS
    `public body` WITH
        `will sign or join the framework agreement`  IS TRUE
        `pays grades the Histadrut represents that are not qualifying` IS FALSE
        `its other agreement`                        IS `no other agreement settling pay rises for 2020-2027`
#ASSERT `the approval a body has` `a local authority signing the agreement` EQUALS `the general approval, with written notice on payment`

`a body with an agreement to 2024` MEANS
    `public body` WITH
        `will sign or join the framework agreement`  IS TRUE
        `pays grades the Histadrut represents that are not qualifying` IS FALSE
        `its other agreement`                        IS `another agreement for part of 1.1.2020-31.12.2027`
#ASSERT `the approval a body has` `a body with an agreement to 2024` EQUALS `a specific approval in advance and in writing`

-- Paid with the March salary (in April), the obligation is fulfilled; not
-- paid by then, it is breached. Deducted in July (June's salary) with the
-- grant still unpaid, fulfilled. On leave until May (first salary in June,
-- month 4) with the grant in month 6: the advance is due by month 5.
#TRACE `paying the advance` (`the illustrated employee` 0.5) AT 0 WITH
    PARTY `the State as employer` DOES `pay the advance` 4300 AT 1
#TRACE `paying the advance` (`the illustrated employee` 0.5) AT 0 WITH
    PARTY `the State as employer` DOES `pay the advance` 4300 AT 3
#TRACE `deducting the advance` 6 AT 0 WITH
    PARTY `the State as employer` DOES `deduct the advance from the salary` AT 4
#TRACE `paying the advance after leave` (`the illustrated employee` 0.5) 3 6 AT 0 WITH
    PARTY `the State as employer` DOES `pay the advance` 4300 AT 4
#TRACE `no contributions on the advance` AT 0 WITH
    PARTY `the State as employer` DOES `make provident-fund contributions on the advance` AT 1
#TRACE `notifying the Wage Controller` `a local authority signing the agreement` AT 0 WITH
    PARTY `a public-sector body` DOES `notify the Wage Controller in writing of the payment` AT 0
